        "id": "515135",
        "date_added": "2026-10-25 08:46:58",
        "twitter_handle": null,
        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "Static loader and delivery verification, 2026-10-25 UTC. SHA-256 verified; 4,938-byte Bash downloader with eleven architecture-labelled blocks. It attempts downloads through wget/curl and BusyBox alternatives, permission changes and execution. The x86_64 block contains an initial URL with an empty port; that malformed literal is not evidence of a separate server. A subsequent correctly formed HTTP delivery URL uses 176.65.139.51:6674 and path /donkeypussy/deathstarx86_64. A bounded read-only GET at 08:44:52 UTC returned HTTP 200, 54,352 bytes and SHA-256 44aaf7dc43cf054f82c676257ad7941fdddeb115b687804164ec673e9f098ad4. Despite its x86_64 filename, the returned file is ELF32, little-endian Intel 80386. Its XOR-0x26 encoded NUL-terminated domain at file offset 47692 decodes to devs.homelabnode.qzz.io, correlating with earlier architecture samples. This establishes one payload relationship; the other named targets were not downloaded or independently family-verified in this review. The script and payload were never executed; no C2 connection was made. URLhaus submission returned already_queued, which is not proof of acceptance, publication or reporter credit."
      }
    ],
